WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.477
A good function should have a clear name, clear inputs, one focused job, and a useful output.

00:00:05.477 --> 00:00:07.762
Also think about predictable problems.

00:00:07.762 --> 00:00:13.012
Should the function validate something?

00:00:13.012 --> 00:00:15.407
Should it handle a conversion error?

00:00:15.407 --> 00:00:19.847
Would a future reader understand its purpose from the name and documentation?

00:00:20.297 --> 00:00:28.120
Small, focused functions are easier to test, easier to reuse, and easier to combine into larger workflows.
